            "body": "Friendly ping for review 🙂 @patrickvonplaten (CODEOWNER for `pixtral*.py`)\n\nStatus notes to make the review easier:\n\n- **Still relevant**: the affected line — `self.freqs_cis[positions[:, 0], positions[:, 1]]` in `VisionTransformer.forward` — is still on `main` (currently `vllm/model_executor/models/pixtral.py:1010`), and no other open PR touches this indexing path.\n- **Small & behavior-preserving**: +6/−1. Indexing the real view and converting back to complex is mathematically equivalent, so CUDA/ROCm behavior is unchanged; it only widens backend portability (e.g. Ascend's `aclnnIndex` does not support `complex64`, which currently blocks Pixtral/Mistral vision models on NPU entirely).\n- The `pre-run-check` failure is just the new-contributor gate (needs a `verified`/`ready` label or ≥4 merged PRs), not a code issue.\n\nHappy to rebase or adjust the implementation if preferred.\n",
